## 2. CERAMIC NETWORK — PIVOTED OUT OF EXISTENCE, TWICE

**Feb 5, 2025** — https://blog.ceramic.network/ceramic-is-joining-textile/ : 3Box Labs merged with **Textile**; Ceramic joins Tableland DB and Basin Network under a mission to build *"an open intelligence network where AI agents can autonomously buy and sell intelligence from each other on-demand."* Claim at the time: Ceramic *"will continue operating with no disruption to current development or customers."* No funding disclosed.

**Apr 17, 2025** — https://blog.ceramic.network/the-future-of-ceramic-focusing-on-recall/ , "The Future of Ceramic: Focusing on Recall". The actual pivot announcement:
- **js-ceramic and ComposeDB are deprecated, effective immediately.**
- **ComposeDB and the Ceramic Anchor Service (CAS) will shut down**, at least one month after Recall's mainnet launch, targeted **mid-2025** (exact date TBD at time of writing).
- *"ComposeDB-dependent apps will break if not migrated to ceramic-one."*
- CAS discontinued; ceramic-one gains "self-anchoring to Recall" — *"fully decentralized timestamping without relying on our centralized CAS or Ethereum L1"* (i.e. the anchor dependency moves from Ethereum to their own token chain).
- Existing data: *"all existing data from ComposeDB remains fully accessible and readable through ceramic-one."*
- Endgame stated plainly: ceramic-one becomes *"stable software under an open MIT license"* for **community maintenance** while the team moves to Recall.

**What Recall actually became:** https://recall.network/ — not a data network. It is an **AI-agent leaderboard and prediction market**: RECALL **ERC-20 token launched on Base, October 2025**; site claims **1.4M users, 175,000 AI agents, 9M curations**, 10 "skill markets" (crypto trading, coding, ethics, safety). Staking, crowdfunding, "Recall Rank."

**Measured decay:**
- blog.ceramic.network **last post: 2025-04-17** (verified via RSS). Nothing in ~17 months.
- **forum.ceramic.network: DNS resolves to 64.227.17.17, connection REFUSED on 443. The forum is down.**
- github.com/ceramicnetwork/js-ceramic: 423 stars, **last push 2025-10-20**.
- github.com/ceramicnetwork/rust-ceramic (`ceramic-one`, the anointed survivor): **51 stars, last push 2026-01-21** — 7½ months idle.
- github.com/ceramicstudio/js-composedb: 94 stars, **last push 2024-07-26**.

Prior technical work now stranded: ceramic-one + Recon protocol (2024-07-16), pairwise sync replacing multicast (2024-07-17), Data Feed API (2024-05-22), node production cost guide (2024-07-05).

**Verdict: did not sustain.** The decentralized data network was deprecated by its own operator inside 15 months of shipping its rewrite, and the company is now a crypto AI-benchmarking token.

