## 3. ORBITDB — ALIVE, BARELY, ON DONATIONS

github.com/orbitdb/orbitdb: **8,800 stars, 595 forks, 25 open issues, last push 2026-05-14, not archived.**
- **v4.0.0 released 2026-05-14** (npm `@orbitdb/core@4.0.0`, 2026-05-14T14:58Z). Prior: 3.0.2 on 2025-05-26.
- **Commit activity: 38 commits in the trailing 52 weeks** (GitHub participation API), concentrated in 3 weeks (12 / 2 / 23 / 1). **Nothing since 2026-05-14 — ~3.7 months idle.**
- **73 contributors all-time**, but the tail is historical: haadcode 1084 commits (long departed), haydenyoung 434 (the current maintainer), shamb0t 148, aphelionz 89. Recent commits are Hayden Young + Alex Potsides (`achingbrain`, an IPFS/libp2p maintainer).
- **Funding: none institutional.** https://orbitdb.org/ : *"OrbitDB is developed by the community for the community so we rely on the community for financial support."* Open Collective + a wall of ~10 crypto donation addresses (ETH, BTC, BCH, LTC, XMR, DOGE, SOL, TRX). A "Floss.fund" link is present. `opencollective.com/orbitdb` returns 200 but the legacy group API returned Not Found — **specific donation totals NOT REACHED.**

**Verdict: one-maintainer project on passive donations, still shipping majors but with months-long gaps.** Note the structural dependency: OrbitDB is IPFS-pubsub-based, so it inherits section 8's problems.

