## 6. BRIAR — NEARLY SHUT DOWN; NOW EXPLICITLY MAINTENANCE-ONLY

**July 9, 2026** — https://briarproject.org/news/2026-maintenance-mode/ , "Briar is in maintenance mode". This is the most direct statement of the funding failure mode in this entire report, quoted in full-relevant part:

> *"For several years we've been trying to find solutions to some of the longstanding issues with Briar, such as high battery usage and unreliable background operation on Android, missing features like account backup and file attachments, and a difficult user experience for adding contacts and communicating offline. We considered completely rebuilding the application from the ground up, or even splitting it into separate applications for online and offline use. Meanwhile, **the project didn't have funding, we were reluctant to look for funding without having a long-term plan, and so we could only work on Briar in our spare time.** **Last year, we decided that we wouldn't realistically be able to solve these issues and so we reluctantly decided to shut down the project.** We worked on releasing a final update for Android and desktop to allow the app to remain functional for as long as possible. In the meantime we were hearing a lot of supportive words… and the app continued to attract new users. So finally we decided to continue the project in maintenance mode. We're only making essential security updates and bugfixes for now."*

So: **decision to shut down taken in 2025; reversed to maintenance-only in July 2026.**

**Release gap: no product news between 2023-08-31 (Briar Desktop 0.6.0-beta) and 2026-07-09** — a ~35-month silence, per the full news index.

**Funding model — grants, all of them, none current:** Small Media Foundation, Open Internet Tools Project, Access Now, **Open Technology Fund**, **Prototype Fund**, Internews, **NLnet Foundation**, **NGI programme**, ISC Project, eQualit.ie. (`briarproject.org/funding/` → 404; funder list is in the maintenance-mode post.) Last funding announcement on the site: **2022-12-05, "Briar Desktop got another round of funding."**

**Published user numbers: NONE.** No user count appears anywhere on briarproject.org. Only qualitative: *"the app continued to attract new users."* Notable adoption datum is negative: **India blocked 14 messengers including Briar, Element and Threema, 2023-05-01** (news.abplive.com / thehindu.com).

Timeline: security audit + public beta 2017-07-21; 1.0 2018-05-09; 1.1 2018-09; 1.2 2019-11; 1.3 2021-06; 1.4 2021-11; Mailbox 2023-06-15; three ETH Zürich security issues fixed 2023-05-24.

**Verdict: the canonical grant-funded P2P messenger reached the end of grant funding, decided to die, and settled for life support.**

