## 7. SECURE SCUTTLEBUTT — THE FLAGSHIP APP LEFT THE PROTOCOL

**Planetary Social: confirmed abandonment of SSB for Nostr.** planetary.social now renders, above its own marketing copy, twice:

> *"We're moving to Nostr. The planetary team has taken our design, app, and philosophy over to Nostr. Our new app is nos.social."*

Planetary was the VC-backed SSB client (HN 2020-01-22: *"Planetary: a VC backed social network built on Scuttlebutt, out of stealth"*). **The site carries no date on the shutdown statement — the exact shutdown date is NOT REACHED.** Repo evidence: `planetary-social/planetary-ios` **202 stars, last push 2025-12-17, not archived**; `planetary-social/nos` (the Nostr successor) **149 stars, last push 2025-07-24**. Note the successor repo is *staler than the abandoned one*.

The Planetary site still advertises the old SSB story unmodified — *"Your data is hosted by your friends through cooperative mutual aid"* — with the Nostr banner pasted over it. It still points users to Manyverse as an alternative SSB client.

**SSB core infrastructure repos are dead:**
- `ssbc/ssb-server` (the pub server itself): 1,703 stars, **last push 2022-06-17** — over 4 years dead.
- `ssbc/ssb-db2`: 50 stars, **last push 2024-04-11**.

**Manyverse survives.** GitHub mirror `staltz/manyverse` 954 stars, last push 2024-08-13; **GitLab `staltz/manyverse` last activity 2026-07-01, 568 stars.** So the one remaining mobile client is still touched, on GitLab, ~2 months ago.

**Attention:** HN mentions of Scuttlebutt since mid-2022 total 8 stories; the top is a generic 231-point link to scuttlebutt.nz (2024-02-23) and a 151-point link to the *Wikipedia article* (2023-01-22). One 2026 item: "Scuttlebutt Genesis" (handbook.scuttlebutt.nz), **1 point, 2026-04-12.**

**The pub-death narrative — PARTIALLY REACHED.** I could not retrieve a first-person account naming the pub collapse. `staltz.com/an-off-grid-social-network.html` does not discuss pubs. scuttlebutt.nz's homepage carries no ecosystem-status page. No "SSB is dying" post was retrievable. **The measured substitute for that narrative is above: the pub server software has had zero commits since June 2022, and the flagship funded client publicly relocated to a protocol with explicit relay servers (Nostr).**

